    "result_text": "There is only one test class in the project, and it passes. \n\nThe change is complete and the test suite is green. Here's what I implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task required assigning a `membershipNumber` formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`Owner.java` model** \u2014 Added a `membershipNumber` field (mapped to a new `membership_number` column) with its getter/setter, following the pattern of the existing derived fields (`customerCode`, `householdId`, `namesakeCount`).\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, after the customer code and registration date are assigned, set the membership number via a new `membershipNumber(...)` helper that formats it as `String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", customerCode, registrationDate.getYear() % 100)` \u2014 zero-padding the two-digit year.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` includes it (MapStruct maps it by name automatically).\n\n4. **Schema files** (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added the `membership_number` column to the `owners` table. This was necessary because the entity persists the field; without it, creates failed with a 500 (`InvalidDataAccessResourceUsageException`).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreMembershipNumberFormat` verifies `customerCode + \"-M\" + yy` equals the returned `membershipNumber`, and the full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
